  "nl_text": "The rschema_0476 database is a schema for a pizza production and sales system. It contains 11 tables, each representing a different aspect of the system.\nThe Customer table contains information about customers, including their address, contact number, customer ID, and name. The Customer ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Raw_Material table contains information about raw materials used in pizza production, including their ID, name, and specification. The Raw Material ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Financial_Record table contains information about financial transactions, including the amount, date, status, transaction ID, and transaction type. The Transaction ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Supplier table contains information about suppliers, including their contact information, supplier ID, and supplier name. The Supplier ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Pizza_Recipe table contains information about pizza recipes, including the raw material ID, recipe ID, and usage amount. The Recipe ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Sales_Order table contains information about sales orders, including the customer ID, expected delivery date, order ID, order status, and foreign key to the Customer table. The Order ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Purchase_Order table contains information about purchase orders, including the order quantity, order status, purchase order ID, raw material ID, supplied quantity, and supplier ID. The Purchase Order ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Product table contains information about products, including the product ID, product name, recipe ID, and foreign key to the Pizza_Recipe table. The Product ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Production_Plan table contains information about production plans, including the order ID, production plan ID, production status, and foreign key to the Sales_Order table. The Production Plan ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Delivery_Record table contains information about delivery records, including the delivery location, delivery record ID, delivery time, order ID, status, and foreign key to the Sales_Order table. The Delivery Record ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe Inventory_Management table contains information about inventory management, including the inventory ID, product ID, quantity, status, and foreign key to the Product table. The Inventory ID is the primary key for this table.\nIn summary, the rschema_0476 database schema is a comprehensive system for managing pizza production and sales, with tables for customers, raw materials, financial transactions, suppliers, recipes, sales orders, purchase orders, products, production plans, delivery records, and inventory management. Each table has its own primary key and foreign keys to other tables as necessary, ensuring referential integrity and entity integrity throughout the system.",
  "gold_question": "The design of the information management system for a pizza shop is as follows:\nThe system includes Customer Management, Sales Order Processing, Production Planning, Raw Material Procurement, Product Inventory Management, Order Delivery, and Financial Records.\nCustomer information comprises Customer ID, Name, Contact Number, and Address.\nSales Order records the customer's order details, including Order ID, Customer ID, Expected Delivery Date, and Order Status.\nProduction Planning determines the production sequence and quantity based on Sales Orders and inventory status, and records the production status.  \nInventory Management tracks the quantity and status of pizzas and raw materials.\nPurchase Orders are used to order raw materials from suppliers, documenting Supplier ID, Raw Material ID, Order Quantity, Supply Quantity, and Order Status.\nDelivery Records track the delivery details of orders, including Delivery Time, Location, and Status.\nFinancial Records manage income and expenses, recording Transaction Type, Amount, Date, and Status.\nAdditionally, the system includes Supplier Information, Pizza Recipes, and Raw Material Details to ensure the smooth progression of production processes.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0476.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0476\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `raw_material` (\n  `raw_material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `specification` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`raw_material_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `financial_record` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `supplier` (\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_information` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supplier_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pizza_recipe` (\n  `recipe_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `raw_material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `usage_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`recipe_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pizza_recipe_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`raw_material_id`) REFERENCES `raw_material` (`raw_material_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_order` (\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `expected_delivery_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `purchase_order` (\n  `purchase_order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `raw_material_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplier_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supplied_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`purchase_order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`raw_material_id`) REFERENCES `raw_material` (`raw_material_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `purchase_order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`supplier_id`) REFERENCES `supplier` (`supplier_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `recipe_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`recipe_id`) REFERENCES `pizza_recipe` (`recipe_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `production_plan` (\n  `production_plan_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `production_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`production_plan_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `production_plan_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `sales_order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `delivery_record` (\n  `delivery_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`delivery_record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `delivery_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`order_id`) REFERENCES `sales_order` (`order_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inventory_management` (\n  `inventory_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`inventory_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inventory_management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
